<title>FRANCE: Alcatel wins $208 million undersea cable deal.</title>
<headline>Alcatel wins $208 million undersea cable deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom said it had obtained a contract worth over 1.2 billion francs for the construction of Atlantis-2, an undersea fibre-optic cable link between South America, Africa and Europe.</p>
<p>Alcatel will supply 90 percent of the contract value, including Synchronous Digital Hierarchy SDH technology and 8,500 km of cable.</p>
<p>Pirelli Cables and Systems will supply 3,500 km of cables.</p>
</text>
